m for states to pass what Florida  just passed a gun violence restraining  order I believe these things we can get  done there's consensus around them  that's step one these other more  contentious issues would be part of step  two but we don't get to step two unless  we show some momentum and some progress  with step one so that's what I've really  been focused on is phase one of this  effort and Senator just to be clear the  bill that the Florida Legislature just  passed it would raise the age for all  gun purchases from 18 to 21 yes or don't  you support that well I would prefer  that it not include shotguns and  bolt-action rifles but but let me be  clear about one thing for people that  are concerned about this it's not  possession so you can be 19 years old  and you know use your father's rifle to  go hunting you just can't be the owner  you can't go in and buy it yourself so  that's an important distinction is for  those out there that are concerned about  that  and we're running out of time but do you  expect the governor to sign that bill  that the Florida Legislature is okay I  believe he'll sign it today  senator Rubio thank you so much for  joining us this morning thank you
 

